# data/ payload stays out of git, but three things must survive a fresh clone:
#   1. the layout documentation
#   2. the 57 manifests -- the reproducibility contract; manifest_hash goes into
#      every MLflow run, and docs/manifest_hash_migration.md exists because
#      their history is scientifically meaningful (~0.7 MB compressed/version)
#   3. the hand-made annotations -- irreplaceable human work (~0.06 MB of text)
#
# Images, video, extracted frames and everything under processed/ stay ignored.
# They are write-once binaries that need a backup, not version control, and
# git-lfs would cost a paid GitHub plan while doubling the local footprint.
#
# Idiom: ignore everything, re-include DIRECTORIES only (trailing slash) so git
# descends into them, then whitelist individual files.
!data/README.md

!data/manifests/
data/manifests/**
!data/manifests/INDEX.md
!data/manifests/*.csv
!data/manifests/*.hash

!data/annotations/
data/annotations/**
!data/annotations/**/
!data/annotations/README.md
!data/annotations/face_pose/README.md
# every .txt under annotations/ is a YOLO label; ** covers both the flat
# labels/ dirs and the split labels/{train,val}/ ones
!data/annotations/**/*.txt
!data/annotations/**/data.yaml
!data/annotations/**/annotations.xml
**/chosen_model/

# training outputs, run scratch, and stray auto-downloaded weights
outputs/
legacy/
optuna_studies.db
/yolo11n-seg.pt
/yolo26n.pt
